  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "parts": [
    {
     "text": "Kusksu (Maltese pronunciation: [ˈkus.ksu]) is a traditional Maltese soup made primarily from seasonal broad beans, small pasta beads, and fresh ġbejniet. Although similar in shape, the small pasta beads, known locally as kusksu, look like couscous, but this one tends to be lighter and fluffier in texture. In contrast, kusksu, which gives the soup its name, is \"miniature pasta\" which is thick and ideal for simmering. Once cooked, the short-cut pasta beads give the soup a creamy and warm texture."
    }
